(7. Viva questions and answers \(10-18\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.357 0.424 0.506 rg
51.0236220472441033 762.5199212598424765 Td
(Be prepared to explain validation and reverse verification.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.11 0.165 0.247 rg
51.0236220472441033 737.0081102362204319 Td
(Q. What does linearly independent mean?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.357 0.424 0.506 rg
51.0236220472441033 721.4175590551180903 Td
(A. No vector in the set can be made from a linear combination of the others. Equivalently, the only combination that gives) Tj
T* (zero uses all-zero coefficients.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.11 0.165 0.247 rg
51.0236220472441033 683.4333070866141497 Td
(Q. How is invertibility related to a basis?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.357 0.424 0.506 rg
51.0236220472441033 667.8427559055118081 Td
(A. A square matrix is invertible exactly when its columns are linearly independent. Its columns then form a basis.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.11 0.165 0.247 rg
51.0236220472441033 643.1813385826771992 Td
(Q. What happens if a basis matrix is singular?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.357 0.424 0.506 rg
51.0236220472441033 627.5907874015747439 Td
(A. It has determinant zero and no inverse. The columns are dependent, so they do not form a basis and the coordinates may) Tj
T* (not be unique. The app stops the transformation.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.11 0.165 0.247 rg
