(Q. What is a linear transformation?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.357 0.424 0.506 rg
51.0236220472441033 520.4411811023621794 Td
(A. A map T that preserves addition and scalar multiplication: T\(x + y\) = T\(x\) + T\(y\) and T\(ax\) = aT\(x\). Matrix multiplication is) Tj
T* (a standard representation of a linear map.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.11 0.165 0.247 rg
51.0236220472441033 482.456929133858182 Td
(Q. Why do we use matrix multiplication?) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.357 0.424 0.506 rg
51.0236220472441033 466.8663779527558404 Td
(A. It composes linear operations and transforms coordinate columns. In P21 = B2^-1 B1, the source basis is applied first,) Tj
T* (followed by the destination inverse.) Tj
